{
  "_doc": "Nightreign arena structure: full mapping of Nightlords, expeditions, Night Boss arenas, and per-expedition NB1/NB2 pool selection.",
  "_version": "v0.24.74",
  "_provenance": "Cross-reference of (a) prior session enumeration of 22 NB arena MSBs from MSB inspection, (b) Sean Martin's PC Gamer per-expedition NB1/NB2 table dated 2025-05-29, (c) EMEVD survey of the v0.24.74 patched bundle.",

  "_terminology": {
    "_disclaimer": "Nightreign uses 'Night Boss' and 'Nightlord' to mean two very different things that sound almost identical. This trips up everyone, including Claude. Keep them straight:",
    "Nightlord": "The Day-3 final boss. 8 total. FIXED per expedition — pick the Tricephalos expedition, you fight Gladius. Each Nightlord has a dedicated arena map (not in m48/m49 range — separate prefix not yet surveyed). C-prefixes: c4900 (Caligo), c7500 (Gladius/Tricephalos), c7510/c7511 (Adel), c7520 (Gnoster), c7540 (Maris), c7560/c7561/c7570 (Libra), c7580 (Heolstor), c7600 (Fulghor).",
    "Night Boss": "The Day-1 or Day-2 encounter. 22 dedicated arena MSBs across m47/m48/m49. POOL-SELECTED per expedition — different runs of the same Nightlord can give different Night 1 / Night 2 fights. Some Dark Souls bosses (Dancer, Nameless King, Smelter Demon, Gaping Dragon, Duke's Dear Freja, Centipede Demon) are script-spawned overlays onto these same 22 arenas, not dedicated MSBs.",
    "Expedition": "A full run. Player picks the expedition (= which Nightlord) at the Roundtable. The expedition name and the Nightlord name often differ (e.g. Tricephalos = expedition, Gladius = Nightlord c-prefix c7500). This is also confusing.",
    "Everdark Sovereign": "Harder version of a Nightlord, unlocked after beating the base version. Same arena, upgraded movesets, +Phase 3."
  },

